#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""lab — the single CLI for a nullsilver research repo.

This is the *only* legal writer of `population.json`, `LEDGER.md` and `events.jsonl`.
Everything the website consumes flows through here, which is why it validates
aggressively and redacts unconditionally: the event feed is public in realtime.

Zero dependencies beyond the Python 3 standard library.

Subcommands (the campaign loop itself lives in tools/lab_campaign.py):
    lab run [campaign.toml]       run the search loop (reap → enforce → dispatch → report)
    lab campaign init|check|status|usage|stop
    lab candidate list
    lab eval <candidate dir>      score a candidate on the hidden search split
    lab job card <candidate dir>  the job card a worker receives
    lab watch start|list|check|kill|close
                                  detached watchdog for long-running work
    lab log <type> --msg ...      append a validated, redacted event
    lab events tail [-n N]        read back the feed
    lab usage [--since --json]    token usage per session, model and role
    lab validate                  lint the repo against the contract
    lab format show|sync|version  the output-format contract for consumers
"""
